From f8948f5723c68188ad4629ac976607fd89e8c212 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <mia.ailab1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 20:06:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 63/63] glm cuda: comm3's copy-engine exchange in prefill3's
 partials and shareGlued; the ranks' fingerprint layout 14

prefill3 moved the pieced exchanges into Forward pieces' partials() and shareGlued(), which a paired step's
exchangeGlue also calls; comm3's TF_GLM_CE_EXCHANGE=1 branch sat in the old inline code, so the merge took it out.
Both now take the piece's index and, with f.ce, push by copy engines into the piece's flag slot, as comm3 did.

A paired step's twin has no f.ce (Engine.view gives it to the registered prompt buffers alone), so its exchanges stay
on NCCL while the first chunk's go by copy engines, through the one room they share (0038). That keeps step order:
- both chunks' exchanges and glue post on one side stream, and a copy-engine put is a cuMemcpyDtoDAsync on it;
- a rank pushes chunk a's next site into the peer's room only after its side stream finished chunk b's split glued
  exchange of the site before, whose NCCL receive completes only once the peer sent, which the peer's side stream does
  after its glue read the room; the other way, b's NCCL receive into a rank's own room follows that rank's own glue
  of a in stream order, after its wait for the peer's push.
The twin's Pieces take their own copy-engine flag slots (ce_slot0 + 2 x max_pieces, as comm3 reserved them), unused
while the twin stays on NCCL.

The fingerprint gained both num3's numerics and prefill3's pair, each of which had taken layout 13: it is 14 now.

